{% comment %}
  Warms the two Searchspring connections that stand between page load and products
  appearing on collection / search pages.

  Those grids are NOT server-rendered. sections/main-collection-product-grid.liquid
  emits an empty <div id="searchspring-content"> and Searchspring Snap fills it in the
  browser, which means the sequence to first product is:

      1. parse HTML
      2. blocking <script src="snapui.searchspring.io/…/bundle.js">   <- cold DNS + TLS
      3. bundle runs, requests <site-id>.a.searchspring.io             <- cold DNS + TLS again
      4. response arrives, preact renders the grid

  Two full connection setups sit on that path, and neither host was preconnected.
  Opening them early removes the handshakes from the critical path. This changes no
  behaviour at all — it only means the connections are ready when Snap needs them.

  Emitted only where Searchspring actually renders (collection, search, 404), so the
  page-wide preconnect budget is not spent on templates that never call it. PageSpeed
  warns above four preconnects; with the theme down to one (fonts.shopifycdn.com) these
  two keep it within budget.
{% endcomment %}

{%- if settings.ss_enable and settings.ss_site_id != blank -%}
  {%- if template.name == 'collection' or template.name == 'search' or template.name == '404' -%}
    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://snapui.searchspring.io" crossorigin>
    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://{{ settings.ss_site_id }}.a.searchspring.io" crossorigin>
  {%- endif -%}
{%- endif -%}
